00:06:27.503 --> 00:06:28.336
I mean, you really are.

00:06:28.336 --> 00:06:29.169
You're not just a friend.

00:06:29.169 --> 00:06:30.002
- Thank you my buddy.

00:06:30.002 --> 00:06:30.835
I paid him to say that

00:06:30.835 --> 00:06:31.860
- No, it's so cool though, like I said,

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:33.780
when the world's collide
as well and you get to do,

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:34.980
well, I feel like I get to do it here.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.992
I get to do the show, but I
still get to involve music.

00:06:36.992 --> 00:06:37.825
- Exactly, exactly.

00:06:37.825 --> 00:06:38.910
- It's nice when that happens.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.710
It breaks up the monotony.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:41.910
It's hilarious you just said whistling,

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:44.010
I'm like, Jocko is actually
whistling on my new album

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:45.900
that's coming out and he's
actually the beginning

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.719
